    "badge": "Best Flavored Tested Powder",
    "category": "Whey protein isolate",
    "description": "Thorne's chocolate and vanilla isolates are both listed in the NSF Certified for Sport registry, which we checked on November 8, 2026. A scoop gives about 21 g of protein at around 100 calories, per the label at the time of writing. For a family that wants a flavored powder a child will drink in milk, with banned-substance and contaminant screening behind it, Thorne is the most straightforward choice, though at a premium price.",
    "pros": [
      "NSF Certified for Sport, both flavors (registry)",
      "Flavored, so easier for a child to accept than unflavored isolate",
      "Short ingredient list",
